      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Hasty Sacrifice",
      "actions": "reaction",
      "category": "defensive",
      "traits": [
        "concentrate",
        "move"
      ],
      "text": "Prerequisite The roughrider is mounted\n\nTrigger The roughrider is targeted with an attack from a creature they can see\n\n---\n\nEffect The roughrider's mount becomes the target of the attack instead. The roughrider must succeed at a DC 5 Flat check check or they fall off their mount and land Prone. If the check is a critical failure, the roughrider also takes 1d6 bludgeoning damage in addition to the normal damage from the fall."
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Powerful Stench",
      "category": "defensive",
      "traits": [
        "aura",
        "olfactory"
      ],
      "text": "30 feet. A creature that enters the area must attempt a DC 30 Fortitude save save. On a failure, the creature is Sickened 2, and on a critical failure, the creature is also Slowed 1 for as long as it is sickened. While within the aura, the creature takes a -2 circumstance penalty to saves to recover from the sickened condition. A creature that succeeds at its save is temporarily immune to all xulgaths' stenches for 1 minute.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "key": "unsupported",
          "foundry": {
            "key": "Aura",
            "radius": 30,
            "slug": "powerful-stench",
            "traits": [
              "olfactory"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Feral Directive",
      "actions": 2,
      "category": "offensive",
      "text": "The xulgath attempts to Command an Animal on their mount, but instead of demanding a specific action such as Stride or Strike, the xulgath gives a general directive, such as to return to camp or to attack a small group the mount can see. The mount and the xulgath each retain 3 actions on their turns, but the mount doesn't change its general tactics until the xulgath uses Feral Directive or Command an Animal again."
    },
